# Without this the whole working directory is sent to the daemon - hundreds of megabytes of
# node_modules and build output - and, worse, `COPY . .` in the builder stage lands the
# host's node_modules on top of the Linux ones installed by `npm ci`. Platform-specific
# binaries (Next's SWC, for one) do not survive that.
node_modules/
.next/
out/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
.env*
